<article class="article">
<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Honda Air Blade vs Automatic Scooter: Hanoi Rental Cost Comparison</h1>
<p>The Honda Air Blade occupies a strange corner of this fleet’s price list. Over days and weeks it is priced exactly like the top of the automatic scooter class, matching the Honda Vision’s verified rates of 200,000 VND per day and 1,000,000 VND per week, yet at the month its flat 1,500,000 VND rate slips beneath the Vision’s published range and settles between the class’s two rungs. It is the only card in this comparison that behaves like the ceiling at short periods and the middle at the longest one.</p>
<p>This guide sets that card against the automatic scooter class rung by rung, using verified figures only, and works out when the Air Blade is a tie with the Vision, when it is a fixed premium over the entry tier, and when its flat month makes it the cheapest step-up machine in the silo. It builds on the guide to <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a>, the main <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> resource, and the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>. Published numbers only, ranges confirmed at the counter, no invented tiers.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">A machine priced like the ceiling</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The verified rates rung by rung</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">What the Air Blade shares with the class</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">The month: a flat figure between tiers</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-5">Short stays: priced at the top</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-6">Monthly rentals: the flat card plays</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-7">Matching the card to your stay</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-8">Questions to settle at the counter</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="sec-1">A machine priced like the ceiling</h2>
<p>Comparing a single machine to its whole category usually means asking what premium it charges over the class. The Honda Air Blade asks a stranger question. At the daily and weekly tiers its verified rates match the very top of the automatic scooter class exactly, 200,000 VND per day and 1,000,000 VND per week, so over short periods it is priced like the premium rung rather than above or below it.</p>
<p>The strangeness arrives at the month. The class’s premium rung, the Honda Vision, is published at 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND per month, while the Air Blade carries a flat 1,500,000 VND monthly rate. Priced like the ceiling for days and weeks, the Air Blade then slips below the ceiling for months, landing between the entry tier and the Vision with a figure that never flexes.</p>
<p>This guide prices that shape honestly. It sets the Air Blade’s verified card against the automatic scooter class rung by rung, using published figures only, and shows where the machine agrees with its category, where it undercuts it, and what a flat monthly figure is worth when every other monthly rate in the comparison is a range.</p>
<h2 id="sec-2">The verified rates rung by rung</h2>
<p>The class first. The entry rung holds the Honda Click and Yamaha Mio at identical verified rates of 150,000 VND per day, 700,000 VND per week and 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND per month, the monthly tier confirmed at the counter. The premium rung holds the Honda Vision at 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week and 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND per month.</p>
<p>The Air Blade’s card reads 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week and 1,500,000 VND per month, the monthly figure quoted flat. Placed against the class, its daily and weekly rows are identical to the Vision’s and 50,000 VND per day above the entry pair, while its monthly row sits below the Vision’s range and above the entry tier’s.</p>
<p>As a picture: at the day and the week the Air Blade shares the ceiling of the class, and at the month it occupies a tier of its own, above the entry machines by 300,000 to 600,000 VND and below the Vision by 300,000 to 500,000 VND. The class structure behind these figures, including how every model stacks up, is charted in the guide to <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a>.</p>
<h2 id="sec-3">What the Air Blade shares with the class</h2>
<p>What the Air Blade shares with the class is the top rung’s short-period pricing. Renters who have decided to pay the step-up rate find the Air Blade and the Vision costing exactly the same money per day and per week, and both costing more than the Click and Mio by the same fixed margins: 50,000 VND per day and 300,000 VND per week.</p>
<p>That agreement simplifies short-stay decisions the same way it does inside the entry pair. For a weekend or a fortnight, the Air Blade versus the Vision is a tie on price, settled by preference and fit at the counter, and the Air Blade versus the Click or Mio is a fixed, legible premium identical to the Vision’s. Nothing about the short-period comparison requires guessing.</p>
<p>What the machine does not share is the class’s monthly habit of quoting ranges. Both class rungs publish their month as a range, the entry tier spanning 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND and the Vision spanning 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND, with the final tier confirmed per rental. The Air Blade is the only card in this comparison whose month is a single number.</p>
<h2 id="sec-4">The month: a flat figure between tiers</h2>
<p>The flat figure changes the monthly landscape. Where the class offers two ranges, the Air Blade’s 1,500,000 VND sits between them: 300,000 to 600,000 VND above the entry tier’s confirmed monthly rates, and 300,000 to 500,000 VND below the Vision’s. In a comparison organized by price tiers, the Air Blade is the middle rung that only exists at the month.</p>
<p>A flat rate also changes what a renter can plan on. A range is honest but open; the exact number arrives at the counter. A flat figure is closed; the published number is the number, the same for every monthly renter, and a month-long budget can be built on it before the trip starts. That certainty is the Air Blade’s quiet product at this tier.</p>
<p>The honest reading cuts both ways. A renter who confirms an entry monthly rate near the floor of its range, say 900,000 VND, pays the entry tier less than the Air Blade’s month, and a renter who prefers the Vision pays it 300,000 to 500,000 VND more. The flat card does not win every comparison; it makes its own outcome knowable in advance, which is a different kind of value.</p>
<h2 id="sec-5">Short stays: priced at the top</h2>
<p>For short stays the Air Blade is priced as the ceiling of the class, and that is the whole story. Per day it costs 200,000 VND, the same as the Vision and 50,000 VND above the Click and Mio. Per week it costs 1,000,000 VND, again level with the Vision and 300,000 VND above the entry pair. No short period produces a price the class has not already seen.</p>
<p>That makes the short-stay decision a familiar one. Between the Air Blade and the Vision, price ties and preference decides. Between the Air Blade and the entry pair, the premium is fixed and legible, and the question is whether the step-up machine’s character and fit are worth 50,000 VND a day to the rider asking the question.</p>
<p>The practical move is unchanged from every comparison in this silo: see the machines. Ask at the shop which of the step-up machines suits your build, routes and plans, confirm availability for your dates, and let the identical short-period pricing remove money from a decision it cannot settle. The counter exists for exactly this conversation.</p>
<h2 id="sec-6">Monthly rentals: the flat card plays</h2>
<p>At the month the Air Blade plays its own card. Its 1,500,000 VND flat rate beats four stacked weeks of its own weekly rate, 4,000,000 VND, by 2,500,000 VND, so the monthly tier is unambiguously the right instrument for a long stay on this machine, exactly as it is on the class’s own cards.</p>
<p>Set against the class, the arithmetic sharpens. Against the entry tier’s confirmed month of 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND, the Air Blade costs 300,000 to 600,000 VND more. Against the Vision’s 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND, it costs 300,000 to 500,000 VND less, a monthly saving attached to a machine that was priced identically to the Vision in every shorter period.</p>
<p>For renters budgeting a long stay, that combination, ceiling pricing at the top of the class for days and weeks, then a flat middle-tier month, is the Air Blade’s specific offer. It is not cheaper than everything, and this guide does not pretend otherwise. It is cheaper than the only machine it ties with at every other tier, and its month is the one number in the comparison that needs no confirmation call.</p>
<h2 id="sec-7">Matching the card to your stay</h2>
<p>By period, the decision reads as follows. A few days: 200,000 VND per day, level with the Vision, and decided by fit against both the entry pair and the Vision. One to three weeks: 1,000,000 VND per week, again level with the Vision, with the daily rate filling the edges at the same rate.</p>
<p>A month: the cards separate, and the Air Blade’s flat 1,500,000 VND becomes the comparison’s known quantity. Confirm the entry tier’s monthly rate if you are weighing a Click or Mio, confirm the Vision’s tier if you are weighing the Vision, and weigh each confirmed number against the Air Blade’s published flat figure.</p>
<p>Beyond a month, only the monthly tier is published for any machine in this comparison, so ask the shop about arrangements for your specific dates rather than extrapolating. Long-stay planning context, including how monthly tiers relate to weekly stacking across the fleet, sits in the main <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> resource.</p>
<h2 id="sec-8">Questions to settle at the counter</h2>
<p>The questions that matter are the ones that turn ranges into numbers. If the Vision is in play, ask where inside its 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND monthly range your rental lands. If an entry machine is in play, ask the same about its 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND range. The Air Blade needs no such question at the month; its figure is flat and published.</p>
<p>For any machine, confirm availability for your dates and the rental’s practicalities: the documents and deposit the shop expects, and what applies to your licence situation, which depends on the licence you hold and where it was issued rather than on the machine. The general answers to these questions are collected in the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>, and your specific case belongs at the counter.</p>
<p>The counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00. One visit covers the whole comparison: the class’s rungs confirmed, the Air Blade’s flat month quoted alongside the Vision’s range, and the machines side by side so the price conversation ends where it should, with a choice made on verified numbers.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions about Honda Air Blade vs automatic scooter rental costs in Hanoi</h2>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>How much does a Honda Air Blade rental cost in Hanoi?</h2>
<p>Verified prices at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu put the Honda Air Blade at 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week and a flat 1,500,000 VND per month. The daily and weekly rates are identical to the Honda Vision, and the flat monthly rate sits below the Vision’s published 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND range.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Is the Honda Air Blade more expensive than an automatic scooter in Hanoi?</h2>
<p>It depends on the period. Per day and per week the Air Blade matches the most expensive automatic in the class, the Honda Vision, at 200,000 VND and 1,000,000 VND, and sits 50,000 VND per day above the Honda Click and Yamaha Mio. At a month its flat 1,500,000 VND is 300,000 to 500,000 VND below the Vision.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>What does an automatic scooter rental cost in Hanoi?</h2>
<p>Verified class rates span 150,000 to 200,000 VND per day, 700,000 to 1,000,000 VND per week and 900,000 to 2,000,000 VND per month. The Honda Click and Yamaha Mio hold the entry rates at 150,000 VND daily, 700,000 VND weekly and 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND monthly, and the Honda Vision tops the class at every tier.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Is the Air Blade’s monthly rate really flat, with no range?</h2>
<p>Yes. The published monthly rate for the Air Blade is a single figure of 1,500,000 VND, quoted flat rather than as a range. The automatic class quotes its months as ranges, 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND for the entry tier and 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND for the Vision, with the final tier confirmed at the counter.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Which is better for a month in Hanoi, the Air Blade or the Vision?</h2>
<p>On price alone the Air Blade is the cheaper month, at 1,500,000 VND flat against the Vision’s 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND range, after the two machines cost identically per day and per week. Comfort, fit and preference decide the rest, and both machines can be compared in person at the shop before you commit.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Where do I confirm monthly rates before renting?</h2>
<p>At the counter of Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00. Ask for the exact monthly tier inside any published range for your dates, and for the flat 1,500,000 VND Air Blade month, and compare the confirmed numbers in the same conversation.</p>
</article>
